# DevOps / GitHub Actions rules
- Workflow names and files follow VAL-COE-01: `ci.yml`, `deploy-dev.yml`, `deploy-staging.yml`, `deploy-prod.yml`, `iac.yml`, `security-nightly.yml`, `cursor-guard.yml`.
- AWS access only through GitHub OIDC (`aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials` with `role-to-assume`); never add AWS access keys.
- Pin every third-party action to a full commit SHA, with the version in a comment.
- Secrets only from GitHub Environments (`${{ secrets.X }}`); never echo secrets.
- Build the Docker image once, tag with the commit SHA, push to ECR, promote the same image.
- Production deploys run only from `v*` tags with the `production` environment (required reviewers).
- Dockerfiles: multi-stage, pinned base image versions, non-root user, no secrets in layers.
- Set `permissions:` to the minimum each job needs.


